# mcp__ripwire_edit_check — ripwire/edit_check

Just edited a symbol? Did its CONTRACT (param count + publicness) change vs git HEAD, and which 1-hop callers are NOW INCOMPATIBLE with the new arity by fixed-arity evidence (not a guess — every folded definition disagrees)? This is call sites worth OPENING, not a proof: call edges are matched by NAME, so a same-named callee this tool does not index can flag a caller that never touches the edited symbol at all, and a clean tree can carry a nonzero incompatible= with nothing edited. status is one of unchanged / new-symbol / contract-change, and callers= is itself a FLOOR — 'no incompatible caller' is not proof of safety either. Fast and targeted; for the same question over a WHOLE diff use quality_delta. symbol = the def name (file:name to disambiguate); at= names the commit compared against. @FILE:LINE line-seeds resolve here too (see find_symbol). limit/offset page the unflagged caller rows only. PRE-APPLY PREVIEW: pass new_body to ask the same question about a replacement that has NOT been written — it is spliced in memory, re-parsed, and the answer carries preview=1. Nothing is written; a payload that does not parse, or does not define the symbol, is refused.

## Schema
```ts
type Args = {
  /** a STRING repo directory */
  path?: string;
  /** an ARRAY of 1..16 repo roots */
  paths?: string[];
  /** the def name you just edited (file:name disambiguates; @FILE:LINE = the def at that line) */
  symbol: string;
  /** OPTIONAL — the replacement definition to PREVIEW rather than apply: the answer then describes the contract AFTER these bytes would be spliced over the symbol, and nothing is written */
  new_body?: string;
  /** a positive integer (omit for the default window) */
  limit?: number;
  /** a non-negative integer (omit to start at row 1) */
  offset?: number;
  /** a STRING legend posture: compact (the default) or full (restores the full legend) */
  legend?: string;
};
```
Execute by writing JSON to xd://mcp__ripwire_edit_check.

